<!--Post: 10007--><!--Time: 1109723408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10007"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 01, 2005 - 4:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Vain&#39;s son says in the article &#40;linked below&#41; that he LATER recognized the picture of him and his mother at his grandmother&#39;s house. <BR> <BR>So, if BTK didn&#39;t work in any photography studio, then where in blazes did he get that picture? <BR> <BR>Did he take it from one of Vain&#39;s relatives when they had security work done in their home by Mr. Denny-Poo? <BR> <BR>Here is the link: <BR><a href="http://www.cnn.com/2005/LAW/03/01/btk.relford/index.html" target=_top>http://www.cnn.com/2005/LAW/03/01/btk.relford/inde x.html</a> <BR> <BR>Here is an excerpt: <BR> <BR>Asked if he knows who was in the picture that the killer showed him, Relford said it was his mother and himself -- something he learned about six years later, when he saw the same photo in his grandparents&#39; home. <BR> <BR>&#34;I told my grandparents, &#39;That&#39;s the picture that that man showed me,&#39;&#34; he said. <BR> <BR>Relford said he would like to ask Rader how he got that picture and &#34;what possessed him to kill my mother and these other innocent folks out here. He had no right.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10007-->
<!--Post: 10127--><!--Time: 1109778447-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10127"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Kayjay<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Kayjay<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 7:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I doubt it was the same picture. When BTK showed the pic to the boy, he didnt recognise it as being his mother. Odd, since the pic couldnt have been more than 5 years old. <BR>I find it hard to believe that the boy would recognize the pic, he had casually seen, six years earlier. To a six year old child, one mother and baby photo would look much the same as the next, particularly if you did not know the subjects.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10127-->
<!--Post: 10425--><!--Time: 1109944236-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10425"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 5:50 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Back in those days, a lot of ladies wore wigs. It was very in style. I remember seeing pics of my mom, and all us kids would laugh, and say, &#34;is that really you?&#34; So, yes, kids can see pics of their mothers from 5 years earlier and not have aclue. <BR>Another thing, think about who you give photos to. <BR>If you have a pic taken at olan mills, or anywhere, you get a lot of them. Im assuming it was a little wallet pic, because I cant see dogshi&#42; breath walking around the neighborhood with a full 8x10. Also, the envelope that was mailed to the media with the baby pic was a regular letter sized envelope, so that baby pic was small.  I have many friends that I have givin pics to over the years. Maybe Shirley gave a pic to a friend, and ....he got it somehow. <BR> <BR>Didnt I read that Mrs Rader babysat, I would give my babysitter a pic of my kid. The story about the babysitting, the people stopped using them, the raders, because he cut the babies hair and gave the mom the hair in an envelope. Freeaky with a capital F. Could the raders have babysat for the Relford children?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10425-->
<!--Post: 10431--><!--Time: 1109951140-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Chiquitah<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Chiquitah<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 04, 2005 - 7:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Oh WOW Itty.  I hadn&#39;t heard that about Denny the Dog Catcher cutting the babies hair!  <BR> <BR>WHY?  WHY?  WHY?  <BR> <BR>SICK  SICK  SICK<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10431-->
<!--Post: 10674--><!--Time: 1110125156-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10674"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Beck<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Beck<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 06, 2005 - 8:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I bet the babies&#39; hair was violating the local &#34;baby hair length ordinance&#34; laws. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
